  {:key :exhaustion :name "Exhaustion" :page 358 :body [[:p "Some special abilities and environmental hazards, such as starvation and the long-term effects of freezing or scorching temperatures, can lead to a special condition called exhaustion. Exhaustion is measured in six levels. An effect can give a creature one or more levels of exhaustion, as specified in the effect’s description."] [:table {:columns ["Level" "Effect"] :rows [[["1"] ["Disadvantage on ability checks"]] [["2"] ["Speed halved"]] [["3"] ["Disadvantage on attack rolls and saving throws"]] [["4"] ["Hit point maximum halved"]] [["5"] ["Speed reduced to 0"]] [["6"] ["Death"]]]}] [:p "If an already exhausted creature suffers another effect that causes exhaustion, its current level of exhaustion increases by the amount specified in the effect’s description."] [:p "A creature suffers the effect of its current level of exhaustion as well as all lower levels. For example, a creature suffering level 2 exhaustion has its speed halved and has disadvantage on ability checks."] [:p "An effect that removes exhaustion reduces its level as specified in the effect’s description, with all exhaustion effects ending if a creature’s exhaustion level is reduced below 1."] [:p "Finishing a long rest reduces a creature’s exhaustion level by 1, provided that the creature has also ingested some food and drink."]]}
  {:key :frightened :name "Frightened" :page 358 :body [[:ul ["A frightened creature has disadvantage on ability checks and attack rolls while the source of its fear is within line of sight."] ["The creature can’t willingly move closer to the source of its fear."]]]}
  {:key :grappled :name "Grappled" :page 358 :body [[:ul ["A grappled creature’s speed becomes 0, and it can’t benefit from any bonus to its speed."] ["The condition ends if the grappler is " [:a {:kind :condition :key :incapacitated} "incapacitated"] " (see the condition)."] ["The condition also ends if an effect removes the grappled creature from the reach of the grappler or grappling effect, such as when a creature is hurled away by the " [:i "thunderwave"] " spell."]]]}
